EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your_publishable_key
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=phc_your_project_token
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Prescription photo hosting. A wa.me link carries text only, so photos are
# uploaded first and the message carries their links. Get a free key at
# https://api.imgbb.com/ — uploads expire; LINK_LIFETIME_DAYS in lib/imgbb.ts
# sets how soon, and explains why the window is finite at all.
# Without it, the prescription screen says so instead of failing silently.
EXPO_PUBLIC_IMGBB_API_KEY=your_imgbb_api_key

# The map the customer drags onto their own building. Android needs a Google
# Maps key or the map renders as an empty grey square; iOS uses Apple Maps and
# needs nothing, and the web build uses OpenStreetMap tiles and needs nothing.
# Enable "Maps SDK for Android" at https://console.cloud.google.com/ and
# restrict the key to the com.golidawayi.app package. Read at build time by
# app.config.js, so set it in the EAS build environment too — not a bundle
# value, hence no EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_android_key

# Address search, and naming the point under the map pin. Optional, but this is
# the single biggest quality difference in the app: OpenStreetMap draws Indore's
# streets without naming most of them, so a pin on a real road comes back as
# "Indore, Madhya Pradesh" and nothing more. Google has the names.
#
# Enable BOTH at https://console.cloud.google.com/ — they are separate APIs:
#   Places API (New)  — the search box
#   Geocoding API     — naming a pin's coordinates
#
# Read in the browser, so it ships in the bundle and MUST be restricted to your
# HTTP referrers. Treat it as public, and keep it separate from the Android maps
# key above, so one key's restriction does not fight the other's.
#
# NOTE: Google refuses every geocoding request with REQUEST_DENIED ("You must
# enable Billing") until the Cloud project has a card on file, even inside the
# free allowance. If you would rather not do that, set the Ola key below instead
# and leave this one unset — the app tries Ola first and never reaches Google.
#
# Without either the app still works: OpenStreetMap names what it can, and falls
# back to the nearest landmark ("Near Gehm Clinic and Research Centre"), which
# needs no key at all.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=your_google_places_key

# Naming a pin's coordinates, without a card. Tried BEFORE the Google key above.
#
# Ola Maps is built in India on Ola's own fleet traces, so it names the colonies
# and unnumbered roads Indore is mostly made of — the exact gap that leaves
# OpenStreetMap answering "Indore, Madhya Pradesh" for a real street. The free
# allowance is 100,000 calls a month at no cost and asks for no payment details
# until you exceed it.
#
# Sign up at https://maps.olakrutrim.com/ and create a Project, then an API key.
#
# Read in the browser, so it ships in the bundle — treat it as public and
# restrict it to your HTTP referrers in the Ola console.
EXPO_PUBLIC_OLA_MAPS_KEY=your_ola_maps_key
